// RosettaForge — Contributing
// ===========================
//
// Rules for adding or changing content. All of it is enforced by convention
// and by the generation pipeline; there is no automated enforcement yet.
//
// File names
// ----------
//
//   * Every tracked file MUST end in .gable. No exceptions.
//   * Challenge path pattern:
//       challenges/<category>/<challenge-id>/<language>/<variant>.gable
//     where variant is `idiomatic` or `edge-case`.
//   * Index shards: index/catalog_NNN.gable.
//
// Challenge specimen contents
// ---------------------------
//
//   Every challenge file must contain:
//
//     1. A stable unique identifier (comment: // id: <id>)
//     2. The problem title and category (comments)
//     3. The reference programming language (comment)
//     4. A verified or explicitly unverified reference-language example
//        (escaped Gable string, and/or comment lines)
//     5. A valid Gable implementation with its own `fn main`
//     6. Representative inputs
//     7. Expected outputs or invariants
//     8. Edge-case coverage
//     9. Time and space complexity explanation
//    10. A meaningful executable test or correctness assertion
//
//   The program must compile (`gable check`) and run (`gable run`), printing
//   PASS/FAIL lines and exiting with the number of failures.
//
// Reference-language snippets
// ---------------------------
//
//   * Escape correctly for Gable: backslash escapes, `\"` for quotes,
//     `\n` for newlines (no multiline string literals).
//   * Be accurate and idiomatic; do not translate character-by-character when
//     the language has a different idiom.
//   * Never mark pseudocode as compilable reference code.
//   * Distinguish verified (validated with the native toolchain) from manually
//      reviewed only. Record verification status in PROGRESS.gable.
//
// Generation pipeline
// -------------------
//
//   * Deterministic and idempotent.
//   * Detect exact duplication and near-duplication; do not count renamed
//     copies as distinct specimens.
//   * Update PROGRESS.gable after every batch.
//   * Never report a phase complete unless acceptance passed.
//
// Verification
// ------------
//
//   gable check <file.gable>
//   gable run <file.gable>
//   gable run core/main.gable check <id>     // prints the check command
//   gable run core/main.gable run <id>       // prints the run command
//
//   Library modules are verified via drivers in verification/ that import them.
//
// .gable-only rule
// ----------------
//
//   Docs, license, and progress records are stored as .gable comments. This
//   prevents GitHub from rendering a conventional README/license; START.gable
//   is the entry point. Do not commit non-.gable source files.
